nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|The way to show a 20 point balanced hand is to double and correct to NT over partner's response. But I think it is fine to be conservative and overcall 1N.|
PG| ***** 42 ***** |


mb|P|mb|P?|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Now I know that both partner and East are weak because I have 18 and West has at least 15. That only leaves 7 HCP at most between North and East. Further, I am sitting behind of the strong hand. In other words. the hand with the strength will play after my hand meaning all of my honors will likely be captured by West. |
PG| ***** 43 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|So I will pass although one could make a case at favorable vulnerability that I should make a takeout double. And if I made that bid North has to bid.|
PG| ***** 44 ***** |


