qx|A4|st||rh||ah|Board 4 IMPs   -   On October 16, 2024|pn|hondo717,IraCT,danpsych,Sputniks|
md|2SJT832HJ9DKJ74C94,SQ975HT86DQT53C82,SA4H5D82CAKQJT763,SK6HAKQ7432DA96C5|sv|b|
mb|P|mb|1C|mb|1H1S|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|On an auction where there is a 1@H overcall when responder has spades there is a special auction. If responder bids 1@S over 1@H that shows 5+ spades. With only 4 spades responder makes a |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=negativedoubles,Negative Double^*N|CP||FP||at|. That is a special auction and does not apply to any other auction. |
PG| ***** 62 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|For example if it goes 1@C-1@D-1@H or 1@S, that only promises a 4-card suit. If it goes 1@C-1@D-dbl, the double promises 4-4 in the majors. While, if it goes 1@C-1@H-Dbl, the double is a |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=negativedoubles,Negative Double^*N|CP||FP||at|.|
PG| ***** 63 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|It is always a |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=negativedoubles,Negative Double^*N|CP||FP||at| whenever responder has not bid (or perhaps passed) and doubles an overcall. So here my 1@S promises 5 (or more) spades.

|
PG| ***** 64 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^^*BA Kib: ^*n Isn't East too strong for 1@H?|
PG| ***** 65 ***** |


cp|8|AT|^^
^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|East has several choices over 1@C. Technically East could make a takeout double first, intending to correct to hearts at her next bid. A double and correct shows a nice 6+ card suit, and at least 16 points or so. Nevertheless, East could bid 1@H but that is admittedly a bit of an underbid.|
PG| ***** 66 ***** |


mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|4C|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I see why North bid 4@C. That eliminates the possibility of playing 3N if I have stoppers in the red suits, admittedly unlikely but possible.|
PG| ***** 67 ***** |


MB|?|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I probably just bid 4@H with the East hand. It is likely East will take at least 8 tricks and has chances for a 9th and 10th if partner has anything.|
PG| ***** 68 ***** |


mb|4H|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|MB|?|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Now the reason I let the bidding, as is, stand is because I have a problem. It is not clear what I should bid. I have one possible defensive trick. To beat the 4@H contract partner needs 3 tricks. And because partner shows long clubs (likely at least 8) it is possible we have no club tricks. Further, I don't want to bid 5@C with 2 hearts.|
PG| ***** 69 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|In Match Points I probably double. But in IMPs it is not as clear what to do. Since I did respond 1@S, partner knows it is likely I have one trick but not much more if I pass. So I will pass and let partner take the blame if we get a bad result. |
PG| ***** 70 ***** |


mb|P|mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|5C|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I agree with 5@C bid. Probably at most down one and 4@H could be making. The reason 5@C at most is down one is if all I have is the @SK we have 10 tricks and I might have something in diamonds as well.|
PG| ***** 71 ***** |


mb|P|mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|D|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I don't understand the double.|
PG| ***** 72 ***** |


AT|^^
^*BEast: ^*nIt is a penalty double.|
PG| ***** 73 ***** |


cp|8|AT|^^
^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I know. but why do you think you have a penalty double. You have no club tricks, partner is not necessarily strong, and you have enough hearts where it is possible you have no heart tricks. I would pass, but if you told me I was not allowed to pass, I would bid 5@H before doubling.|
PG| ***** 74 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^^B@2^*BWest: ^*nMy partner can not be weak.|
PG| ***** 75 ***** |


cp|8|AT|^^
^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Yes, so what? If your partner thinks she is beating it, she can double. As a matter of fact, it turns out you are right but just barely only because we lose a heart.|
